# Local tooling state, never part of the package
# Local agent-tooling state. `.nexus/` is listed by its real directory name on
# purpose: the generic rename swept it out of here, and the very next commit
# nearly published four files of internal tool state to a public repository.
# An ignore pattern is not disclosure — every repo ignores its editors' and
# tools' scratch directories — and not ignoring one is how those directories
# get committed.
.nexus/
.refcertify/
.serena/

# `npm pack` output. A published tarball in the repo is both noise and a stale
# copy of the package.
*.tgz
